// expect: compile_error
// expect-error: E300

// GAP — owner: B2, scoped to 0.0.8.
// Measured 2026-09-11: error[E300] Argument Type Mismatch at the second call.
//
// `forward` has no annotation and no constraint *of its own* — it only calls
// something constrained. That is enough to withhold generalization: G5's rule
// requires that the definition "raised no constraint of its own", and the
// obligation `dbl` raises passes through `forward` as if it were its own.
//
// The exclusion is deliberate rather than incidental. Generalizing a
// forwarding helper was tried and produced `E491` in four
// examples/aoc/2024/day06* programs, where the helper forwarded a value whose
// field the callee projected — so the receiver reached the callee unpinned.
//
// Adding the annotation `fn forward<a: Num>(x: a) -> a` fixes this file today.

fn dbl<a: Num>(x: a) -> a { x + x }

fn forward(x) { dbl(x) }

fn main() with IO {
    print(forward(2))
    print(forward(2.5))
}
